ORDINANCE V OF 1997
ORDINANCE V OF 1997
COTTON STANDARDIZATION ORDINANCE, 1997
2. Definitions.‑‑In this Ordinance unless there is
anything repugnant in the subject or context,‑‑
(a) "bale" means a
pressed package of cotton of prescribed size and density;
(b) "Board" means the
Board of Directors of the Institute constitution under section 5;
(c) "certified ginning
factory" means a ginning factory granted a standardization certificate
under section 13;
(d) "Chairman" means
Chairman of the Board;
(e) "Classer" means a
person trained in cotton classing and having obtained a certificate issued by
the Institute;
(f) "cotton" means
the post harvest seed cotton and lint cotton;
(g) . "cotton
standard" means classification and grading of seed cotton and lint cotton;
(h) "ginner" means
any natural or legal person responsible for managing ginning factory;
(i) "grade" means a
grade of cotton established under this Ordinance;
(j) "institute" means
the Pakistan Cotton Standards Institute constituted under this Ordinance;
(k) "irregular
cotton" means below grade, mixed grades or staple lengths, discoloured
cotton, cotton waste and salvaged cotton;
(1) "member" means
member of the Board;
(m) "prescribed"
means prescribed by rules made under this Ordinance;
(n) "season" means the
cotton year as defined in the Cotton Control Ordinance, 1966 (W.P. Ordinance XX
of 1966);
(o) "seed cotton box"
means a box prepared by the Institute and containing a grade of seed cotton;
(p) "standard box"
means a box prepared by the Institute and containing a standard for cotton
lint; and
(q) "Technical
Officer" means a person qualified in cotton classification selected by the
Institute as Technical Officer.
